From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: k114s-integration <integration@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:51:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/37] drm/apple: hold brightness requests at the panel's
 floor

The nits backlight (H17P, firmware 27) accepts every level from 0 to
apple,max-brightness, and a brightness-only present carries it to the
firmware as written. 0 is presented as 0 nits. That is the level DPMS
off uses to darken the panel, so a write of 0 to the backlight device
looks like a display that turned itself off, with only another
brightness write to bring it back.

Read an optional apple,min-brightness from the panel node, in the same
nits as apple,max-brightness. A request below it, zero included, is
raised to it, and the backlight device reads the raised level back.
Blanking, DPMS off and suspend are not requests and still present zero.
A level reported by the loader below the floor stays until the first
request. Without the property, or with one that is not below the
ceiling, nothing changes. The DAC path of older firmware does not read
it.

KUnit: backlight_floor_test. Run on a build host through stand-in
headers (28 cases pass, and the new case fails with the floor removed);
not run under KUnit.

K114s (MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro) integration patch, not from
upstream. Hardware-untested: compiled, not booted on any machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>

(r3c: re-cut on integration/aurora 677be395; only the dcp_set_brightness() hunk moved, where the base now passes a local 'suspended' instead of the BL_CORE_SUSPENDED test.)
